 "about_text": "Design Festa Gallery is a rental exhibition space in Harajuku, Tokyo, open to any artist regardless of experience or genre. Founded in spring 1998 on the concept of creating an open place for anyone expressing themselves, the gallery now spans two buildings, GALLERY WEST and GALLERY EAST, with over 70 spaces including more than 20 exhibition rooms of varying sizes and a Wall Paint Space for mural work. Exhibitions change daily, covering solo debuts, group shows, workshops, film screenings and product showcases. The gallery draws an average of over 300 visitors a day, about 30% of them from overseas, fostering direct interaction between exhibitors and the public. It is also used as a filming location and is affiliated with the biannual Design Festa art event.",
